n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-8 \\\\  & =9-(17-9) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2-17 \\\\  & =[43-17\\cdot 2]\\cdot 2-17 \\\\  & =43\\cdot 2-17\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =43\\cdot 2+17\\cdot (-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=2$ and $v=-5.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=2+(-5)=-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152184 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4caf9fc6-9247-5807-84de-208b731116e7" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extended Euclidean Algorithm When the Two Numbers are Not Coprime"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6077b7eb-756b-552b-b943-a113e194ff8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410956} {:answer/id #uuid "80620617-47d4-5fff-998f-1dbae8bb3e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410963} {:answer/id #uuid "c32ab406-9856-51a3-a3f5-bd4ec204acf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410977} {:answer/id #uuid "d2af4861-828f-59f3-bec2-6ae0170f80c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410979} {:answer/id #uuid "f060b56c-3f61-5a69-9915-cbd94852b8b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2af4861-828f-59f3-bec2-6ae0170f80c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410979} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c39c5e-8a07-5782-972e-e1ea5abb9373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29de6c34-4477-5dd6-9882-390e0598c400" :question/math-academy-id "q-78470" :question/problem "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $28u+16v=\\text{gcd}(28,16).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}28 & = & 16\\cdot 1 & + & 12 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 16 & = & 12\\cdot 1 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 12 & = & 4\\cdot 3 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(16,28)=4.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =28-16 \\\\ 4 & =16-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =16-12 \\\\  & =16-(28-16) \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2-28 \\\\  & =28\\cdot (-1)+16\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-1$ and $v=2.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-1)+2=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152184 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4caf9fc6-9247-5807-84de-208b731116e7" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extended Euclidean Algorithm When the Two Numbers are Not Coprime"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020f98df-ce27-5f83-a183-d790fdb0efb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410944} {:answer/id #uuid "025792a9-1418-5ed0-bd75-63fdf48048ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410945} {:answer/id #uuid "047f5cfa-c319-5769-a5d9-38ab5eac2e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410946} {:answer/id #uuid "5e46fd5a-2cae-5e32-9a58-53a8ac056701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410955} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e226a7-3802-529c-a38f-3a53dfbd2df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "047f5cfa-c319-5769-a5d9-38ab5eac2e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410946} :answer-field/id #uuid "38098c07-0137-58e9-b523-6a7aeb39ec12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef7dfe31-fa62-51d2-b435-2d5f9267bf87" :question/math-academy-id "q-79848" :question/problem "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $64u+28v=\\text{gcd}(64,28).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}64 & = & 28\\cdot 2 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 28 & = & 8\\cdot 3 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 8 & = & 4\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(64,28)=4.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =64-28\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4 & =28-8\\cdot 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =28-8\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =28-(64-28\\cdot 2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =28\\cdot 7-64\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =64\\cdot (-3)+28\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-3$ and $v=7.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-3)+7=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c5f369-1196-5ace-9450-815a4ee2cc8f" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extended Euclidean Algorithm When the Two Numbers are Coprime"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26070e7e-e2f2-538f-a981-409b7228a780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410948} {:answer/id #uuid "3132dcdb-547b-5f5a-85ac-f3d9b7acfe30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410950} {:answer/id #uuid "4844b534-18e6-52ed-9d01-29f0d3eda197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410954} {:answer/id #uuid "731a5592-7314-5a88-8d25-9787cd947c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410962} {:answer/id #uuid "c204f2e3-9422-550e-81c1-05aa17cb715b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26070e7e-e2f2-538f-a981-409b7228a780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410948} :answer-field/id #uuid "9998cffe-b044-5c0e-8d8d-808f7ebe4f34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f595bdf1-0020-53f4-bd59-1e7fad6ce48b" :question/math-academy-id "q-79901" :question/problem "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $70u+31v=\\text{gcd}(70,31).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}70 & = & 31\\cdot 2 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 31 & = & 8\\cdot 3 & + & 7 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 8 & = & 7\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(70,31)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =70-31\\cdot 2 \\\\ 7 & =31-8\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =8-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =8-7 \\\\  & =8-[31-8\\cdot 3] \\\\  & =8\\cdot 4-31 \\\\  & =[70-31\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4-31 \\\\  & =70\\cdot 4-31\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =70\\cdot 4+31\\cdot (-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=4$ and $v=-9.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=4+(-9)=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c5f369-1196-5ace-9450-815a4ee2cc8f" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extended Euclidean Algorithm When the Two Numbers are Coprime"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2709c658-cd3e-5e8b-b07f-16cf2388e15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410949} {:answer/id #uuid "62a127f8-b980-5984-80d8-aa47e7479f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410958} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f2fca7-3768-5b96-ad99-d94d7bcbae25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410969} {:answer/id #uuid "d04712dd-ae0a-541d-aa43-0ec8c6212a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410978} {:answer/id #uuid "e0202928-b98c-52f5-9374-736765c43c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62a127f8-b980-5984-80d8-aa47e7479f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410958} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eec11f2-7132-57a2-9c39-dc49f5d75e62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5854fb1f-195a-5978-bfc0-db75a9114381" :question/math-academy-id "q-79902" :question/problem "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $79u+35v=\\text{gcd}(79,35).$ What is the value of $u+v?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}79 & = & 35\\cdot 2 & + & 9 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 35 & = & 9\\cdot 3 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 9 & = & 8\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(79,35)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =79-35\\cdot 2 \\\\ 8 & =35-9\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =9-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-8 \\\\  & =9-[35-9\\cdot 3] \\\\  & =9\\cdot 4-35 \\\\  & =[79-35\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4-35 \\\\  & =79\\cdot 4-35\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =79\\cdot 4+35\\cdot (-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=4$ and $v=-9.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=4+(-9)=-5.\n$$"}]}
